  - IFC
  - embodied carbon
  - net zero
abstract: >-
  CladBench v1 is an open benchmark of 536 questions across twelve categories of
  UK and EU built-environment practice, covering Building Regulations, EPC
  trajectory estimation, IFC entity reasoning, BMS sensor anomaly
  classification, retrofit prioritisation, BREEAM credit eligibility, thermal
  comfort diagnosis, CIBSE technical guidance, material and embodied-carbon
  specification, energy-bill anomaly detection, net-zero pathway reasoning and
  regulatory cliff-edge reasoning. Seven contemporary models were evaluated,
  with all rubric-graded answers marked by two judges that are not themselves
  evaluated. Reference answers are labelled by evidential status: 196 verified
  against a primary source, 257 resting on multi-model agreement, and 83
  recorded as not usable as ground truth with a stated reason. All 3,752
  per-question model outputs are released so the scores can be recomputed
  without access to any evaluated model.
